<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sundiata Keita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1255</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Sundiata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sundiata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keita-dynasty">Keita</a> was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>, who died c. 1255. Around 1235 he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumanguru-kante">Sumanguru Kanté</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kirina">Battle of Kirina</a>. Accounts of the Mali Empire credit him with uniting twelve kingdoms and establishing the empire's governance.</p></div>
